{
  "0": "Across all four datasets, increase the recent-four-state pooling weight from 0.2 to 0.3, using 0.7*current_state + 0.3*recent_mean. The two-state regression motivates testing stronger smoothing while retaining four-state context. Pool only observed causal prefix states and read the final real position. Keep features, embeddings, backbone, scoring, loss and optimizer fixed; synchronize readout metadata and predictor writer.",
  "1": "Across all four datasets, reduce each causal block's residual-update multiplier from 0.5 to 0.35. The improvement at 0.5 motivates testing whether further damping preserves useful input information through the six-block stack. Keep block count, dilation schedule, embeddings, features, history/readout, scoring, loss and optimizer fixed. Update residual-scale metadata and predictor compatibility checks.",
  "2": "Across all four datasets, replace sqrt(normalized_log_training_count) with normalized_log_training_count**0.75 in the existing input-frequency feature, retaining attenuation 1-0.3*feature. This weakens attenuation for moderately frequent items while preserving maximum attenuation for the most frequent items. Derive counts solely from training interactions and retain zero for unseen items. Keep learned embeddings, topology, readout, scoring, loss and optimizer fixed; use the saved feature buffer at inference.",
  "3": "Across all four datasets, increase tied item-embedding and matching hidden width from 48 to 52, propagating only required tensor-shape changes. Since widths 40 and 64 regressed, this tests a modest capacity increase near the incumbent without changing input/output sharing. Keep initialization scheme, features, causal block structure, history/readout, dot-product scoring, loss and optimizer fixed. Ensure checkpoint metadata and the predictor writer load width 52 consistently."
}
